                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4d5a4c4e-bdd0-3312-be75-7727a64d1953",
                        "entry_id": "39d14029-4033-3754-a33b-5257a38efc43",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Resembling or characteristic of a blast or explosion."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a984cb8d-626e-4aca-a7dc-449f7874f6a7",
                                "sense_id": "4d5a4c4e-bdd0-3312-be75-7727a64d1953",
                                "text": "How could a lodger make blasty noises without a gramophone to drown his shame ... ?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "41cf9944-8e93-4a6c-8582-7e8aef5d8515",
                                "sense_id": "4d5a4c4e-bdd0-3312-be75-7727a64d1953",
                                "text": "Personally, I wouldn't have the muzzle-brake on the end of a rifle barrel—particularly not a rifle with such a blasty calibre as the .270."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "966dd468-1afc-4908-99d8-0029058f999c",
                                "sense_id": "4d5a4c4e-bdd0-3312-be75-7727a64d1953",
                                "text": "And the kid picked out this pomegranate-colored rug with all these colorful swooshes and he called it the \"blasty rug,\" and the mom kept pulling him over to this plain brown rug and saying, \"This will match your bedspread, Henry.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "17002f01-2dd1-4dd3-8456-590fb926b296",
                                "sense_id": "4d5a4c4e-bdd0-3312-be75-7727a64d1953",
                                "text": "\"Why don't I get a cool blasty thing?” Alex demanded."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a676d1c5-2c2c-37ae-90ca-e504c74ec202",
                        "entry_id": "39d14029-4033-3754-a33b-5257a38efc43",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Extremely loud."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "44d0ef98-b7b3-45c5-b9db-e0e9cc8aa9fd",
                                "sense_id": "a676d1c5-2c2c-37ae-90ca-e504c74ec202",
                                "text": "The recording is for the most part clean and bright, with only an occasional blasty forte marring the otherwise excellent sound."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "04fc27d5-ce95-489d-aa2e-679be0f89642",
                                "sense_id": "a676d1c5-2c2c-37ae-90ca-e504c74ec202",
                                "text": "Roland's arrangement of the Ellington-Strayhorn piece captures the feeling of the original but invests it with the Kenton sound by employing the band's predictable blasty trombones and its typical screaming trumpets ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ea31238-e269-47ed-864d-d7e7e70941de",
                                "sense_id": "a676d1c5-2c2c-37ae-90ca-e504c74ec202",
                                "text": "Not merely do the scrunching squeaks of the break, the blasty trumpet whistle , the slamming of doors , and the squalling of children bewilder his brain and bedeafen his ears, but the iron tyrant enchains and confuses his eyes ."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fd037b1d-53cc-323f-8cae-c0cee3fe6bc1",
                        "entry_id": "39d14029-4033-3754-a33b-5257a38efc43",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Affected by blasts; gusty."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "11e6b58b-6c7a-400f-8071-de2da666ed73",
                                "sense_id": "fd037b1d-53cc-323f-8cae-c0cee3fe6bc1",
                                "text": "Thus passed the first afternoon of my retour by the Mountaineer, and the next day being blasty and bleak, nobody was in a humour either to tell or to hear stories;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7e20e0e3-6677-4802-a1f3-21b07481f678",
                                "sense_id": "fd037b1d-53cc-323f-8cae-c0cee3fe6bc1",
                                "text": "In the morning the weather was blasty and sleety , waxing more and more tempestuous, till about mid-day, when the wind checked suddenly round from the nor-east to the sou-west, and blew a gale, as if the prince of the powers of the air was doing his utmost to work mischief."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7819b3ad-ec7c-44ec-86d6-539a12229bc3",
                                "sense_id": "fd037b1d-53cc-323f-8cae-c0cee3fe6bc1",
                                "text": "Thus far we have come through the winter, on this bleak and blasty shore of the Irish Sea, where, perhaps, the drowned body of Milton's friend Lycidas might have been washed ashore more than two centuries ago."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c20190f6-16c1-4d74-8c0b-4c3f01f7ed08",
                                "sense_id": "fd037b1d-53cc-323f-8cae-c0cee3fe6bc1",
                                "text": "The day after we reached hom was very fine, and we were out with the children as long as the sun shone; but the next morning Dorothy roused me from my sleep with \"Aunt! it is time to get up, it is a blasty morning — it does blast so!\" and the next morning with \"It is a haily morning — it hails so hard! \" And this blasty and haily and snowy weather continued till last Friday, and during the first three or four days I was half killed by it; and I thought our house, with its plastered walls, half-carpeted floors, and half-furnished rooms, the coldest place in the world."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "469c4cb9-b9eb-35a3-8471-c80990aabb7a",
                        "entry_id": "39d14029-4033-3754-a33b-5257a38efc43",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Given to outbursts; blustery."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "44495d4f-95dc-4380-8746-cf2ff08ee0c4",
                                "sense_id": "469c4cb9-b9eb-35a3-8471-c80990aabb7a",
                                "text": "I told him it was not, and then he said, \"Pooh, pooh, Carey; you know what a windy, blasty fellow Chisholm is , and it is not worth while to take any more notice of it, or say anything about it. \""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b37368f6-5cb6-4377-9297-90eaa7bdf4c0",
                                "sense_id": "469c4cb9-b9eb-35a3-8471-c80990aabb7a",
                                "text": "Once I had a temper cheerful, and my home was full of peace, and you heard no wailing tearful from my wife or aunt or niece; but for months I've been as nasty as a bear with festered dome, and I said things blanky- blasty when I had to write a pome."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fc0fe907-5b94-3654-b68a-90fd8cf1636a",
                        "entry_id": "39d14029-4033-3754-a33b-5257a38efc43",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Causing or displaying blast (blight) or injury"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c0011614-ea70-4cc3-a7d8-1399a52aa0f1",
                                "sense_id": "fc0fe907-5b94-3654-b68a-90fd8cf1636a",
                                "text": "The floor, the pews, the stripped-bare altar are strewn with leaves, twigs, orange needles from the blasty boughs of spruce trees."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd5baf26-bec4-493c-81a6-4e87bf3385f8",
                                "sense_id": "fc0fe907-5b94-3654-b68a-90fd8cf1636a",
                                "text": "The Yearling took in soprano Dolores Wilson, leprechaun David Wayne, and some blasty kids."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
